{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795252398,"nonce":"0r8n010N8IpQmhuW+2nrkqcxyW0=","title":"Record treadmill vibration logs and add them as test fixtures","message":"The first test run (2026-11-18) showed that a Garmin records the footpod's cadence of 0 as 0 spm\ninstead of falling back to wrist cadence, which also zeroes running power and running dynamics.\nCadence is a mandatory RSC field, so it cannot be left out.\n\nThe speed estimate only has to beat 0 spm. Measuring cadence with an accelerometer is the main focus\nonce the estimate is checked on a run.\n\nRecord accelerometer logs on a treadmill at several paces (walking and running) and add them as\nengine test fixtures.","files":null}]}